Author: QIU023 <yiqiaoqiu@hotmail.com>
Date:   Tue Jul 21 05:05:32 2026 +0000

    moe: preserve router shard placement in routing-map scatter (fixes TP+EP)
    
    CORE common-MoE change (not experiment-specific; helps any MoE under
    TP+EP). Under TP+EP the router outputs are DTensors sharded on the token
    dim; DTensor has no scatter strategy preserving Shard(dim=1) -- in-place
    scatter_ errors, and out-of-place scatter redistributes to Replicate,
    which breaks the downstream Partial(sum) token-count contract that
    RoutedExperts declares. Do the one-hot scatter on the local shard and
    rewrap with the router's placement. Unblocks TP+EP and the full 4D
    FSDP+TP+EP+PP mesh (verified on the K3 debug model, 8 GPU). Non-DTensor
    path unchanged; suite 79 green.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

